{"name":"Terrazzo Tan","hex":"#be8973","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"terrazzo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A faux-marble material used for flooring and countertops."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrazzo"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Terrazzo","blocks":[{"text":"Terrazzo is a composite material, poured in place or precast, which is used for floor and wall treatments. It consists of chips of marble, quartz, granite, glass, or other suitable material, poured with a cementitious binder, polymeric, or a combination of both. Metal strips often divide sections, or changes in color or material in a pattern. Additional chips may be sprinkled atop the mix before it sets. After it is cured it is ground and polished smooth or otherwise finished to produce a uniformly textured surface. \"Terrazzo\" is also often used to describe any pattern similar to the original terrazzo floors.\nModern forms of terrazzo include polished concrete."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Terrazzo_entryway.jpg/330px-Terrazzo_entryway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrazzo"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg/500px-Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg/500px-Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the most well known examples of terrazzo flooring is the Hollywood Walk of Fame.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHollywood_Walk_of_Fame_(7960322318).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Pima1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Pima1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Terrazzo with stylized Native-American design at the Hoover Dam","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APima1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG/500px-Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG/500px-Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Terrazzo wall at the Gamla stan metro station, Stockholm","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG"}],"sounds":{"tan":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f0/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tan.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f0/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tan.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tan.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common